◆The heavy burden of a county hospital

Though the smallest of Korea&rsquo;s local public hospitals, Jinan Medical Center carries the burden of healthcare for the entire county. Its ER runs 24/7, sustained by a handful of doctors taking shifts. The financial weight falls squarely on county coffers: Jinan County spends about 4 billion KRW annually on the hospital&rsquo;s operation. Without this, it could not cover wages, maintenance, and equipment costs.

A medical center official said, &ldquo;We must keep ER and essential departments running, but the operating cost pressures are severe for a hospital this small. It&rsquo;s also very difficult to recruit doctors to rural areas.&rdquo;

Although labeled a county hospital, it is truly a burden too heavy for the county alone. Yet it cannot be abandoned, as it remains the sole place residents rely on every day.


